{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00954",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.06,
      "end_seconds": 17.1,
      "duration_seconds": 16.04,
      "text": "Hi, thank you for seeing me. I hit my head two days ago, and I've had a headache since, and I wanted to make sure it's nothing serious."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 20.02,
      "end_seconds": 25.12,
      "duration_seconds": 5.1,
      "text": "Of course. Tell me exactly what happened. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 26.69,
      "end_seconds": 43.43,
      "duration_seconds": 16.74,
      "text": "I was on a ladder at work, about eight feet, slipped on the third rung and came down on my right side, my head hit the concrete. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 45.9,
      "end_seconds": 48.65,
      "duration_seconds": 2.75,
      "text": "Did you lose consciousness?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 50.08,
      "end_seconds": 61.34,
      "duration_seconds": 11.26,
      "text": "No, I don't think so. I was dazed for a minute, but I remember everything, including the ambulance guy asking my name."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 64.19,
      "end_seconds": 67.41,
      "duration_seconds": 3.22,
      "text": "Good. Tell me about the headache."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 69.43,
      "end_seconds": 81.92,
      "duration_seconds": 12.49,
      "text": "It's a dull ache, all across the back and the right side. Worse in the afternoon. It started the same evening."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 84.55,
      "end_seconds": 86.27,
      "duration_seconds": 1.72,
      "text": "Any nausea?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 87.14,
      "end_seconds": 93.3,
      "duration_seconds": 6.16,
      "text": "A bit queasy, mostly the first day. Still a little today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 94.17,
      "end_seconds": 97.48,
      "duration_seconds": 3.31,
      "text": "Is the light bothering you? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 99.55,
      "end_seconds": 105.2,
      "duration_seconds": 5.65,
      "text": "A little, yes, I've kept the blinds down. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 107.97,
      "end_seconds": 113.47,
      "duration_seconds": 5.5,
      "text": "Is there anything you've been taking for it? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 116.42,
      "end_seconds": 121.33,
      "duration_seconds": 4.91,
      "text": "Not yet. I didn't want to mask anything. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 124.15,
      "end_seconds": 129.03,
      "duration_seconds": 4.88,
      "text": "Good thinking. Do you have any health conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 130.33,
      "end_seconds": 136.61,
      "duration_seconds": 6.28,
      "text": "Migraines, since college. And high blood pressure, but it's controlled with exercise."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 139.07,
      "end_seconds": 142.15,
      "duration_seconds": 3.08,
      "text": "What do you do for work?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 143.31,
      "end_seconds": 150.6,
      "duration_seconds": 7.29,
      "text": "I'm a construction foreman. Mostly on sites, rarely on ladders, which is the irony."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 161.32,
      "end_seconds": 169.49,
      "duration_seconds": 8.17,
      "text": "Let me take your numbers. Blood pressure 128 over 80, pulse 68, and oxygen 98 percent."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 170.88,
      "end_seconds": 173.38,
      "duration_seconds": 2.5,
      "text": "Is that fine? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 185.62,
      "end_seconds": 192.59,
      "duration_seconds": 6.97,
      "text": "That's fine. Let me look at your head. Tell me when it's tender."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 194.72,
      "end_seconds": 198.48,
      "duration_seconds": 3.76,
      "text": "There. Ow. That's the spot. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 200.59,
      "end_seconds": 212.15,
      "duration_seconds": 11.56,
      "text": "There's a bruise and a tender swelling on the right side at the back of your head, about the size of an egg."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 214.49,
      "end_seconds": 217.05,
      "duration_seconds": 2.56,
      "text": "I haven't looked. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 227.77,
      "end_seconds": 234.43,
      "duration_seconds": 6.66,
      "text": "Now follow my finger with your eyes, without moving your head."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 235.37,
      "end_seconds": 238.0,
      "duration_seconds": 2.63,
      "text": "Like this? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 239.07,
      "end_seconds": 247.56,
      "duration_seconds": 8.49,
      "text": "Your pupils are equal and react to light, and your eye movements are normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 248.98,
      "end_seconds": 251.85,
      "duration_seconds": 2.87,
      "text": "That's good, right? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 264.4,
      "end_seconds": 272.36,
      "duration_seconds": 7.96,
      "text": "Very. Now walk the line to the door and back, heel to toe."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 275.27,
      "end_seconds": 278.78,
      "duration_seconds": 3.51,
      "text": "That's a bit wobbly. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 280.58,
      "end_seconds": 284.22,
      "duration_seconds": 3.64,
      "text": "It's steady enough. Your balance is normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 285.65,
      "end_seconds": 287.54,
      "duration_seconds": 1.89,
      "text": "Phew. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 289.31,
      "end_seconds": 294.6,
      "duration_seconds": 5.29,
      "text": "Any weakness, numbness, or trouble speaking since the fall?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 296.62,
      "end_seconds": 305.69,
      "duration_seconds": 9.07,
      "text": "No, nothing like that. My speech is normal, and my arms and legs feel fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 306.51,
      "end_seconds": 322.31,
      "duration_seconds": 15.8,
      "text": "Here's what I think. This looks like a concussion, but with a head injury like this, I can't rule out a small bleed inside the head."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 324.84,
      "end_seconds": 327.1,
      "duration_seconds": 2.26,
      "text": "A bleed? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 329.71,
      "end_seconds": 338.63,
      "duration_seconds": 8.92,
      "text": "It's unlikely, but I'd rather be safe. I'd like to arrange a CT scan of your head today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 341.58,
      "end_seconds": 345.69,
      "duration_seconds": 4.11,
      "text": "Okay. How long does it take? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 347.44,
      "end_seconds": 360.27,
      "duration_seconds": 12.83,
      "text": "The scan takes minutes, the wait is longer. I'd also like to start paracetamol, 1 gram, every six hours, for the headache."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 362.53,
      "end_seconds": 364.74,
      "duration_seconds": 2.21,
      "text": "No ibuprofen? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 365.49,
      "end_seconds": 373.92,
      "duration_seconds": 8.43,
      "text": "Avoid ibuprofen for now. And rest, no work, no screens for a day or two."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 375.24,
      "end_seconds": 377.33,
      "duration_seconds": 2.09,
      "text": "Fair enough. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 379.79,
      "end_seconds": 391.04,
      "duration_seconds": 11.25,
      "text": "If the headache gets worse, you vomit, or you feel confused or very drowsy, come back to the emergency department immediately."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 391.88,
      "end_seconds": 394.38,
      "duration_seconds": 2.5,
      "text": "Understood. Thank you. ~"
    }
  ]
}
